cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  counterfactual-legislatures: what legislatures would look like
  under different electoral systems
message: >-
  If you use this software or the datasets derived from it,
  please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Bruno
    family-names: Parga
repository-code: 'https://github.com/brunoparga/counterfactual-legislatures'
abstract: >-
  Redraws legislatures under electoral systems other than the ones
  actually used. The first phase reproduces and extends the shortest
  splitline districting of the United States across the 2000, 2010 and
  2020 censuses, under three House-size rules and four choices of
  whether the District of Columbia and Puerto Rico are apportioned.
  The districting engine is a port of Ivan Ryan's 2007 autodistrict;
  everything else is original.
keywords:
  - redistricting
  - electoral systems
  - apportionment
  - proportional representation
  - gerrymandering
  - shortest splitline
license: Apache-2.0
